    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1572">

                <pb facs="1314" n="1210" xml:id="pg1210"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 723.2515/245.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to Chile to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santiago, Chile</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 9, 1911</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Senator Walker Martinez introduced yesterday in the Senate motion providing
                    election of one Senator from Tacna-Arica and one Deputy for Tacna and Tarata and
                    one Deputy for Arica, in the general elections to be held next March. Press
                    applauds motion.</p>
                <p>Extracts published from Peru newspapers charge that there is systematic plan of
                    driving Peruvian citizens out of the Provinces. Manager of the Peruvian Bank of
                    Tacna, who was also the so-called Peruvian intendente, left a few days ago at
                    the instance of Chilean general commanding there. Chilean forces engaged in
                    maneuvers will remain in the vicinity of Tacna until distribution of garrisons
                    is decided. General staff leaves on the 15th for the north, to be absent, it is
                    stated, three weeks.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
